---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Wayline from '../components/Wayline.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Chapel — Don't Lose Your Way" description="The Chapel is a quiet gathering place inside Don't Lose Your Way: leave an anonymous reflection, read the reflections of others, and stand for a while in a room where people understand. The lyric-making Chapel is still being built.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>The Chapel</h1>
      <p>A creative space where visitors can write a few words about what they are feeling and transform those emotions into phrases, lyrics, or songs.</p>
      <p>Through the Chapel experience, feelings can be transformed into words, phrases, lyrics, or songs that give emotion a voice.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <Wayline />
    </div>

    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>The Chapel is open — as a gathering place</h2>
      <p>The lyric-making Chapel is still being built, carefully, on a foundation that can keep it safe. For now, the Chapel opens its doors as something simpler: a quiet room where you can leave a reflection and read the reflections of others who have stood where you stand.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-forum" aria-label="The Chapel gathering place">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="peer-note" role="note">
        <p><strong>This is a peer space, not therapy,</strong> and it is not monitored around the clock. Every reflection is read by a person before it appears here. If you are in crisis right now, please reach out: <a href="tel:988">call or text 988</a>, or <a href="sms:741741">text TALK to 741741</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="rooms-heading" id="rooms-heading">Choose a room</h2>
      <div class="rooms" role="group" aria-labelledby="rooms-heading" id="rooms"></div>
      <p class="room-desc" id="room-desc" aria-live="polite"></p>

      <div id="posts" class="posts" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="posts-status" id="posts-status">Opening the room…</p>
      </div>

      <div class="form-wrap">
        <h2 id="form-heading">Leave a reflection</h2>
        <p class="reply-context" id="reply-context" hidden>
          You are responding to a reflection in this room.
          <button type="button" class="link-btn" id="reply-cancel">Cancel and start fresh</button>
        </p>

        <form id="chapel-form" novalidate>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-room">Room</label>
            <select id="f-room" name="room"></select>
          </div>

          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-body">Your reflection</label>
            <textarea id="f-body" name="body" rows="5" maxlength="1200" required aria-describedby="body-count body-help"></textarea>
            <p class="field-row">
              <span id="body-help">Say it the way it is tonight. Plain words are enough.</span>
              <span id="body-count" class="count">0 / 1200</span>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-signoff">Sign-off <span class="optional">(optional, one word)</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="f-signoff" name="signoff" maxlength="24" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="signoff-help" />
            <p class="field-note" id="signoff-help">A name you choose for this room only. Leave it blank to stay simply anonymous.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
            <label>Website <input type="text" id="f-website" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
          </div>

          <p class="privacy-line">Anonymous by design: no account, no email, nothing that identifies you. Every reflection is read by a person before it appears. <a href="/legal/community-moderation">How moderation works</a> · <a href="/legal/crisis-protocol">Crisis protocol</a></p>

          <p class="form-error" id="form-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
          <button type="submit" class="submit-btn" id="submit-btn">Share my reflection</button>
        </form>

        <div class="panel panel-thanks" id="panel-thanks" tabindex="-1" hidden>
          <h3>Thank you.</h3>
          <p>Your reflection is with us now. A person reads every one before it appears here, so it may take a little time. You are not the only one.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="panel panel-crisis" id="panel-crisis" tabindex="-1" hidden>
          <h3>Please stay.</h3>
          <p>What you wrote tells us you may be hurting in a way this room cannot hold. Your reflection was not saved, and you are not in trouble — we just want real help within your reach right now.</p>
          <p class="crisis-actions">
            <a class="cbtn" href="tel:988">Call or text 988</a>
            <a class="cbtn cbtn-alt" href="sms:741741">Text TALK to 741741</a>
          </p>
          <p>Free, confidential, 24/7. When you are ready, this room will still be here.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="panel panel-rephrase" id="panel-rephrase" tabindex="-1" hidden>
          <h3>One small ask.</h3>
          <p>This room asks for gentler words. What you have to say matters here, and it lands better without language that targets people. Please reword your reflection and try again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- is:global on purpose: the room buttons, post cards, and respond buttons
       are created by the page script at runtime and never carry Astro's scoped
       style attribute, so scoped rules would not reach them. These styles ship
       only in this page's bundle. -->
  <style is:global>
    .section-forum { padding-top: 0; }
    .peer-note {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-strong-bg);
      background: var(--surface);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }
    .peer-note p { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 300; }
    .peer-note strong { color: var(--text); }

    .rooms-heading { margin-top: 0; }
    .rooms { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 1rem 0 0.75rem; }
    .room-btn {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px;
      padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 9999px;
      background: transparent; color: var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 0.9375rem; cursor: pointer;
    }
    .room-btn:hover { color: var(--text); background: var(--surface); }
    .room-btn[aria-pressed="true"] { color: #ffffff; background: var(--accent-strong-bg); border-color: var(--accent-strong-bg); }
    .room-desc { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 300; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; min-height: 1.6em; }

    .posts { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
    .posts-status { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 300; }
    .post {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-strong-bg);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .post-body { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text); white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; }
    .post-meta { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.875rem; }
    .respond-btn {
      margin-top: 0.75rem; min-height: 44px; padding: 0.5rem 0.25rem;
      background: none; border: 0; color: var(--accent-tint);
      font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 0.9375rem; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline;
    }
    .replies { margin-top: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
    .reply {
      border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
      padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
    }
    .reply .post-body { font-size: 1rem; }

    .form-wrap {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
    }
    .field { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .field label { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text); }
    .field .optional { font-weight: 300; color: var(--muted); }
    .field select, .field textarea, .field input[type="text"] {
      width: 100%;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .field select { min-height: 44px; }
    .field textarea { resize: vertical; }
    .field-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 300; }
    .field-note { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 300; }
    .count { white-space: nowrap; }
    .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
    .privacy-line { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 300; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
    .reply-context { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 300; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
    .link-btn { background: none; border: 0; color: var(--accent-tint); font: inherit; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; min-height: 44px; padding: 0.25rem; }
    .form-error { color: var(--accent-tint); font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .submit-btn {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px;
      padding: 0.625rem 1.5rem; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px;
      background: var(--accent-strong-bg); color: #ffffff;
      font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9375rem; cursor: pointer;
    }
    .submit-btn[disabled] { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }

    .panel {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      background: var(--surface);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    .panel h3 { margin-top: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--text); }
    .panel p { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .panel p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .panel-crisis { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-strong-bg); }
    .crisis-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
    .cbtn {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px;
      padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 9999px;
      background: var(--accent-strong-bg); color: #ffffff;
      font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9375rem; text-decoration: none;
    }
    .cbtn-alt { background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--accent-tint); color: var(--accent-tint); }
  </style>

  <script>
    // The Chapel gathering place — anonymous, moderated, safety-screened.
    // Spine: cc3po-ops Supabase. Anon key is public by design; the tables'
    // RLS does the protecting (anon reads APPROVED only, inserts PENDING only,
    // no update/delete). Nothing displays here that a person has not approved.
    const SPINE_URL = 'https://cdrcgmdvepxwsbqaifxv.supabase.co';
    const SPINE_ANON_KEY =
      'eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImNkcmNnbWR2ZXB4d3NicWFpZnh2Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NzM1MDY4MDksImV4cCI6MjA4OTA4MjgwOX0.pKWLWvsSimTOMkpaXKKrLJESrQEMUayUU1c9ANzr1Dc';

    const ROOMS = [
      { key: 'tonight', label: 'Where I stand tonight', desc: 'For whatever tonight is, exactly as it is.' },
      { key: 'letter', label: 'The Letter', desc: 'For the words you wrote, or almost wrote — and the morning after.' },
      { key: 'quiet-spiral', label: 'The Quiet Spiral', desc: 'When it starts quietly — the withdrawing, the going numb, the smile that costs.' },
      { key: 'wall', label: 'The Wall', desc: 'The systems that don\u2019t see you: paperwork, waiting rooms, doors that don\u2019t open.' },
      { key: 'breaking-point', label: 'The Breaking Point', desc: 'The night everything broke — told from the side of still being here.' },
      { key: 'aftermath', label: 'The Aftermath', desc: 'After the headlines, when it gets quiet and the work of staying begins.' },
      { key: 'breaking-cycle', label: 'Breaking the Cycle', desc: 'What you are building so it does not repeat — for you, or for your kids.' },
    ];

    // Deterministic two-tier safety screen (v2, 2026-11-25 — Carlos approved
    // softening the v1 blunt rule). The lists and the algorithm are IDENTICAL
    // to the database trigger (qa/screen-v2.sql), which re-runs the screen
    // server-side, so Tier 1 content is never stored even if this page is
    // bypassed. The model is never part of the safety system; there is no
    // model here at all.
    //   TIER 1 (never stored; visitor gets the crisis panel): method content
    //     in any tense, and crisis vocabulary with a present-tense desire,
    //     intent, plan, or farewell signal — or a bare imminence marker with
    //     no past framing.
    //   TIER 2 (stored as pending, flagged 'crisis_terms' for the human
    //     moderator): crisis vocabulary in past-tense / survivor /
    //     third-person / help-seeking framing. Nothing publishes without a
    //     person approving it, so testimony waits in the same queue as
    //     everything else — it is no longer turned away at the door.
    const METHOD_TERMS = [
      'overdose', 'overdosed', 'slit my wrists', 'cut my wrists', 'hang myself',
      'hanged myself', 'shoot myself', 'shot myself', 'jump off a', 'jump off the',
      'jumped off a', 'jumped off the',
      'sobredosis', 'ahorcarme', 'colgarme', 'dispararme', 'cortarme las venas',
    ];
    const CRISIS_TERMS = [
      'kill myself', 'suicide', 'suicidal', 'end my life', 'end it all',
      'want to die', 'self harm', 'cut myself', 'hurt myself', 'no reason to live',
      'suicidio', 'suicida', 'matarme', 'quitarme la vida', 'acabar con mi vida',
      'acabar con todo', 'hacerme daño', 'no quiero vivir', 'quiero morir',
      'quiero morirme',
    ];
    const PRESENT_STRONG = [
      'want to die', 'want to kill myself', 'want to end my life',
      'going to kill', 'going to end it', 'going to end my life',
      'about to kill', 'about to end', 'i have a plan', 'my plan is',
      'plan to kill', 'plan to end', 'goodbye forever', 'saying goodbye',
      'last message', 'cant go on', 'cant do this anymore',
      'dont want to be here anymore', 'thinking about suicide',
      'thoughts of suicide', 'feeling suicidal', 'feel suicidal', 'i am suicidal', 'im suicidal',
      'quiero morir', 'quiero morirme', 'no quiero vivir', 'quiero matarme',
      'quiero acabar con mi vida', 'quiero terminar con mi vida',
      'voy a matarme', 'voy a quitarme la vida', 'voy a acabar con mi vida',
      'tengo un plan', 'mi plan es', 'ultimo mensaje',
      'ya no puedo mas', 'no puedo mas', 'pensando en el suicidio',
      'pensando en suicidarme', 'me siento suicida',
    ];
    const PRESENT_TIME = [
      'tonight', 'right now', 'today', 'esta noche', 'ahora mismo', 'hoy',
    ];
    const PAST_FORMS = [
      'wanted to die', 'tried to kill myself', 'tried to end my life', 'ended it all',
      'tried to die', 'used to want to die', 'used to cut myself',
      'used to hurt myself',
      'quise morir', 'quise quitarme la vida', 'intente matarme',
      'intente quitarme la vida', 'intente suicidarme', 'pensaba en morir',
      'pensaba en el suicidio', 'queria morir', 'queria morirme',
    ];
    const PAST_MARKERS = [
      'last year', 'last month', 'last week', 'last night', 'years ago',
      'months ago', 'back then', 'at the time', 'when i was', 'used to',
      'el ano pasado', 'el mes pasado', 'la semana pasada', 'anoche',
      'hace anos', 'hace meses', 'hace un ano', 'en ese momento', 'cuando tenia',
    ];
    const ABUSE_TERMS = [
      'kill all', 'death to', 'hate all', 'fuck you',
      'nigger', 'nigga', 'faggot', 'cunt', 'retard', 'kike', 'spic',
      'wetback', 'tranny',
    ];

    const MIN_INTERVAL_MS = 90000;
    const LAST_KEY = 'dlywChapelLastSubmit';

    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const roomsEl = $('rooms'), descEl = $('room-desc'), postsEl = $('posts'),
      form = $('chapel-form'), roomSel = $('f-room'), bodyEl = $('f-body'),
      signoffEl = $('f-signoff'), honeyEl = $('f-website'), countEl = $('body-count'),
      errorEl = $('form-error'), submitBtn = $('submit-btn'),
      replyCtx = $('reply-context'), formHeading = $('form-heading');

    let activeRoom = 'tonight';
    let replyParent = null; // { id, room } when responding to a reflection

    function normalize(s) {
      return (s || '')
        .toLowerCase()
        .normalize('NFD')
        .replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, '')
        .replace(/[^a-z0-9 ]+/g, ' ')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();
    }
    function screened(text, terms) {
      const hay = ' ' + normalize(text) + ' ';
      return terms.some((t) => hay.includes(' ' + normalize(t) + ' '));
    }
    function hasTerm(hay, terms) {
      return terms.some((t) => hay.includes(' ' + normalize(t) + ' '));
    }
    // Two-tier crisis classification — mirrors the database trigger exactly.
    // Returns 1 (Tier 1: never store, crisis panel), 2 (Tier 2: store as
    // pending with the moderator flag), or 0 (no crisis vocabulary).
    function crisisTier(text) {
      const hay = ' ' + normalize(text) + ' ';
      if (hasTerm(hay, METHOD_TERMS)) return 1;
      const crisisHit = hasTerm(hay, CRISIS_TERMS) || hasTerm(hay, PAST_FORMS);
      if (!crisisHit) return 0;
      if (hasTerm(hay, PRESENT_STRONG)) return 1;
      const pastFraming = hasTerm(hay, PAST_FORMS) || hasTerm(hay, PAST_MARKERS);
      if (!pastFraming && hasTerm(hay, PRESENT_TIME)) return 1;
      return 2;
    }
    function looksSpammy(text) {
      const links = (text.match(/https?:\/\//gi) || []).length;
      return links >= 2 || /(.)\1{11,}/.test(text);
    }

    async function spineInsert(table, row) {
      const res = await fetch(`${SPINE_URL}/rest/v1/${table}`, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
          apikey: SPINE_ANON_KEY,
          Authorization: `Bearer ${SPINE_ANON_KEY}`,
          Prefer: 'return=minimal',
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(row),
      });
      if (!res.ok) {
        let detail = '';
        try { detail = JSON.stringify(await res.json()); } catch {}
        throw new Error(`insert failed ${res.status} ${detail}`);
      }
    }

    // Safety events carry metadata only — room, category, time. Never the
    // visitor's words, never anything that identifies them.
    function logSafetyEvent(category) {
      spineInsert('dlyw_chapel_safety_events', {
        room: replyParent ? replyParent.room : roomSel.value,
        category,
      }).catch(() => {});
    }

    function showPanel(id) {
      for (const p of ['panel-thanks', 'panel-crisis', 'panel-rephrase']) {
        $(p).hidden = p !== id;
      }
      if (id) $(id).focus();
    }
    function showError(msg) {
      errorEl.textContent = msg;
      errorEl.hidden = !msg;
    }

    function fmtDate(iso) {
      try {
        return new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' });
      } catch { return ''; }
    }

    function postCard(post, isReply) {
      const art = document.createElement('article');
      art.className = isReply ? 'reply' : 'post';
      const body = document.createElement('p');
      body.className = 'post-body';
      body.textContent = post.body;
      const meta = document.createElement('p');
      meta.className = 'post-meta';
      meta.textContent = `— ${post.signoff ? post.signoff : 'Anonymous'} · ${fmtDate(post.created_at)}`;
      art.append(body, meta);
      if (!isReply) {
        const btn = document.createElement('button');
        btn.type = 'button';
        btn.className = 'respond-btn';
        btn.textContent = 'Respond to this reflection';
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => setReply(post));
        art.append(btn);
      }
      return art;
    }

    async function loadRoom(room) {
      activeRoom = room;
      descEl.textContent = ROOMS.find((r) => r.key === room)?.desc || '';
      for (const b of roomsEl.querySelectorAll('.room-btn')) {
        b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', b.dataset.room === room ? 'true' : 'false');
      }
      postsEl.innerHTML = '';
      const status = document.createElement('p');
      status.className = 'posts-status';
      status.textContent = 'Opening the room…';
      postsEl.append(status);
      try {
        const q = new URLSearchParams({
          select: 'id,created_at,room,body,signoff,parent_id',
          room: `eq.${room}`,
          order: 'created_at.desc',
          limit: '100',
        });
        const res = await fetch(`${SPINE_URL}/rest/v1/dlyw_chapel_posts?${q}`, {
          headers: { apikey: SPINE_ANON_KEY, Authorization: `Bearer ${SPINE_ANON_KEY}` },
        });
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error('load failed');
        const rows = await res.json();
        postsEl.innerHTML = '';
        const tops = rows.filter((r) => !r.parent_id);
        const replies = rows.filter((r) => r.parent_id);
        if (!tops.length) {
          const empty = document.createElement('p');
          empty.className = 'posts-status';
          empty.textContent = 'No reflections in this room yet. Yours could be the first voice someone reads tonight.';
          postsEl.append(empty);
          return;
        }
        for (const top of tops) {
          const card = postCard(top, false);
          const mine = replies
            .filter((r) => r.parent_id === top.id)
            .sort((a, b) => new Date(a.created_at) - new Date(b.created_at));
          if (mine.length) {
            const wrap = document.createElement('div');
            wrap.className = 'replies';
            for (const r of mine) wrap.append(postCard(r, true));
            card.append(wrap);
          }
          postsEl.append(card);
        }
      } catch {
        postsEl.innerHTML = '';
        const err = document.createElement('p');
        err.className = 'posts-status';
        err.textContent = 'The room is quiet right now — reflections could not be loaded. Please try again in a moment.';
        postsEl.append(err);
      }
    }

    function setReply(post) {
      replyParent = { id: post.id, room: post.room };
      roomSel.value = post.room;
      roomSel.disabled = true;
      replyCtx.hidden = false;
      formHeading.textContent = 'Respond to a reflection';
      bodyEl.focus();
      form.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
    }
    function clearReply() {
      replyParent = null;
      roomSel.disabled = false;
      replyCtx.hidden = true;
      formHeading.textContent = 'Leave a reflection';
    }

    // Build room buttons + form room options.
    for (const room of ROOMS) {
      const b = document.createElement('button');
      b.type = 'button';
      b.className = 'room-btn';
      b.dataset.room = room.key;
      b.textContent = room.label;
      b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', room.key === activeRoom ? 'true' : 'false');
      b.addEventListener('click', () => { clearReply(); roomSel.value = room.key; loadRoom(room.key); });
      roomsEl.append(b);
      const opt = document.createElement('option');
      opt.value = room.key;
      opt.textContent = room.label;
      roomSel.append(opt);
    }
    roomSel.value = activeRoom;
    roomSel.addEventListener('change', () => loadRoom(roomSel.value));
    $('reply-cancel').addEventListener('click', clearReply);
    bodyEl.addEventListener('input', () => { countEl.textContent = `${bodyEl.value.length} / 1200`; });

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (ev) => {
      ev.preventDefault();
      showError('');
      showPanel(null);

      // Honeypot: a filled invisible field means a bot. Appear to succeed;
      // store nothing, log nothing.
      if (honeyEl.value) { showPanel('panel-thanks'); form.reset(); countEl.textContent = '0 / 1200'; return; }

      const body = bodyEl.value.trim();
      let signoff = signoffEl.value.trim().replace(/\s+/g, '');
      if (signoff.length > 24) signoff = signoff.slice(0, 24);
      if (body.length < 1) { showError('Please write a few words first — even one honest line is enough.'); bodyEl.focus(); return; }

      const last = Number(localStorage.getItem(LAST_KEY) || 0);
      if (Date.now() - last < MIN_INTERVAL_MS) {
        showError('One reflection at a time — please wait a moment before sharing another.');
        return;
      }

      const combined = `${body} ${signoff}`;
      const tier = crisisTier(combined);
      if (tier === 1) {
        localStorage.setItem(LAST_KEY, String(Date.now()));
        logSafetyEvent('crisis');
        showPanel('panel-crisis');
        return;
      }
      if (screened(combined, ABUSE_TERMS) || looksSpammy(body)) {
        localStorage.setItem(LAST_KEY, String(Date.now()));
        logSafetyEvent('abuse');
        showPanel('panel-rephrase');
        return;
      }

      submitBtn.disabled = true;
      try {
        await spineInsert('dlyw_chapel_posts', {
          room: replyParent ? replyParent.room : roomSel.value,
          body,
          signoff: signoff || null,
          parent_id: replyParent ? replyParent.id : null,
          status: 'pending',
          // Tier 2 testimony carries the moderator flag; the database
          // trigger recomputes it server-side either way.
          screen_flag: tier === 2 ? 'crisis_terms' : null,
        });
        localStorage.setItem(LAST_KEY, String(Date.now()));
        form.reset();
        countEl.textContent = '0 / 1200';
        clearReply();
        roomSel.value = activeRoom;
        showPanel('panel-thanks');
      } catch (err) {
        // The database trigger re-runs the crisis screen; if it stopped the
        // write, treat it exactly like a screen hit on this page.
        if (String(err && err.message).includes('screened')) {
          logSafetyEvent('crisis');
          showPanel('panel-crisis');
        } else {
          showError('Your reflection could not be sent just now. Please try again in a moment — this room will be here.');
        }
      } finally {
        submitBtn.disabled = false;
      }
    });

    loadRoom(activeRoom);
  </script>
</Layout>
